From: Cristodcgomez <cristo.c.mc@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] opp: tolerate missing ICC providers (dace bring-up)

dev_pm_opp_of_find_icc_paths returned -EPROBE_DEFER when the ICC provider
(qnoc-monaco) was not loaded -> sdhci/kgsl/drm/geni deferred and no eMMC.
Without qnoc (whose registration triggers a hard reset to EDL, a pending
cause), the ICC paths stay empty and the drivers run without bw voting (bus
with ABL rates).
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [dace bring-up]
Signed-off-by: Cristodcgomez <cristo.c.mc@gmail.com>
---

diff --git a/drivers/opp/of.c b/drivers/opp/of.c
index 3028353af..f7f27ada2 100644
--- a/drivers/opp/of.c
+++ b/drivers/opp/of.c
@@ -491,12 +491,16 @@ int dev_pm_opp_of_find_icc_paths(struct device *dev,
 	for (i = 0; i < num_paths; i++) {
 		paths[i] = of_icc_get_by_index(dev, i);
 		if (IS_ERR(paths[i])) {
-			ret = PTR_ERR(paths[i]);
-			if (ret != -EPROBE_DEFER) {
-				dev_err(dev, "%s: Unable to get path%d: %d\n",
-					__func__, i, ret);
-			}
-			goto err;
+			/* dace bring-up: qnoc-monaco is not loaded (its
+			 * registration triggers a hard reset to EDL). Leave the
+			 * ICC paths empty instead of deferring: the drivers probe
+			 * without bw voting (the bus keeps the bootloader rates).
+			 * Consumers tolerate path==NULL (sdhci-msm already does:
+			 * 'Failed to get bus_scale data' is non-fatal). */
+			dev_info(dev, "%s: icc path%d not available (%ld) - no bw voting\n",
+				__func__, i, PTR_ERR(paths[i]));
+			kfree(paths);
+			return 0;
 		}
 	}
 
